Net income, EBIT, and Free Cash Flow valuation bases use the explicitly reconciled TTM figures in Section 4. Book value uses the latest balance sheet, and market values use the observed closing price.

**Interpretation framework:** P/E and Earnings Yield are one parent-earnings claim expressed in inverse forms and must be counted once. P/B uses parent book equity; Free Cash Flow Yield uses a net-income-share proxy for parent attribution; and lease-exclusive EV / reported operating income uses reported EBIT. The methods are not averaged or ranked.

